-- title:
--   Two points off the finite chart in the geometric p-fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $5 \le p$, and let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ (in the bottom universe). Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p`, the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}/\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the divisor expansions at level $p$, and let $j =$ `IgusaScheme.jFull p` be the element of $F$ given by the $q$-expansion $jq$. Then `DRModel p` is the two-chart integral model $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\ \mathbb{Z}\ F\ j$, the pushout of the two maps from the middle affine scheme to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $\mathbb{Z}$-chart algebras attached to $j$ and to $j^{-1}$, and `DRModel.toBase p` is the induced structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$. The assertion is that in the pullback of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, i.e. in the geometric fibre of the model over $k$, there exist two points $y_1 \ne y_2$ whose images under the underlying map of the first projection both fail to lie in the open subset of `DRModel p` obtained as the image of the whole of the $j$-finite chart under the morphism `TwoChartIntegralModel.ιFin ℤ F j`.
--
--   The two points are the reductions modulo $p$ of the cusps $\infty$ and $0$ of $X_0(p)$, which lie over $j = \infty$ and hence outside the $j$-finite chart of the Deligne–Rapoport integral model. The statement is used, together with the count of points of each labelled component of the fibre lying over $j = \infty$, to locate the supersingular crossing points inside the $j$-finite chart when the component-and-depth data of the fibre is assembled.
-- source:
